# Lockfile policy (kit-backlog B5.1, supersedes polish-2026-10-02 P5): package-lock.json IS committed. CI's bats job
# installs these tools with `npm ci` (audit A6), so the whole tree, transitive dependencies included, is the one the
# lockfile pins and a drift shows up as a reviewed diff. The direct pins in package.json stay exact; refresh the
# lockfile with `npm install --prefix build-n4-module-kit/toolbelt/eslint` only when a pin changes, and commit both.
# Lifecycle scripts never run: CI passes --ignore-scripts (neither tool needs one); local runs use
# `npm ci --prefix build-n4-module-kit/toolbelt/eslint --ignore-scripts` too.
node_modules/
